Because they're not fun in the same way.
These days, when I play, I choose a role at random but immediately quit if  
it is either one I've already ascended or one I don't want to play.
I play wizards as well as knights, but no rogue (or cavemen, for that  
matter).
And I really don't think that you can qualify wizards and knights as  
"parity". They have a very different playing style, both in the early and  
late game. Some people will consider wizards as fun and knights as boring,  
or the other way around (and rogue as the funniest role so I'm silly not  
playing them).

If cavemen are really less liked (eg significantly less played on public  
servers), then indeed it could be interesting to make them more fun to  
play. This does not mean easier to play, obviously. Toursits are pretty  
hard to play in the early game and yet still a popular choice (as far as I  
can tell).

A new special ability specific to one class would certainly not make it  
more "like" the other classes, on the contrary I would say.


I think all role should be "brought to parity" from an enjoyment of  
playing them perspective. Certainly not from a difficulty of playing them  
perspective and even less from a style perspective (I really don't like  
all these STR or other strategy game where you have several  
races/nations/clans/... whose only difference is the design and names of  
units but (almost) no real in game difference (Warcraft 1, Dune,  
typically)).

